## Session 56 summary

**Confirmed state at start:** `cache_coherency` now PASSES; sole ship-gate blocker is `posix_semantics_multi16` (`elapsed>600s`) from FS shutdowns under the 16-node shared-dir storm (`tests/reset4.sh 16` + `tests/repro_agi_unlink_storm.sh 16 6`).

**Killed the sess55 red herring.** sess55's "dir dirent bytes overwrite an inode cluster" (on-disk clobber) framing was wrong — my P56-DIRWR-OVER-DISKINODE write-submit probe fired **0×** like M1/M2. The real signature: P54-DIRBLK-PROBE shows the **on-disk** dir block is valid (XDB3, owner ok, CRC ok), while the shutdown is **in-core** corruption (`xfs_buf_verify_write` / `xfs_dir3_block_verify` / `xfs_dabuf_map HOLE`).

**PROVEN ROOT (RULE-4, probe fired on the exact shutting-down dir):** A dir grows block→leaf when a peer adds dirents — block 0 flips XDB3→XDD3 on disk, the inode gains a 2nd extent. The evict-ring arms `MXFS_IF_DIR_RELOAD` on peers but **does not bump `i_dlm_dir_gen` when gen==0**. The dir-EX **fast-path** acquire refresh keyed only on the gen, ignoring the flag → a fast-path mkdir/remove reached `xfs_dir2_format` with a stale 1-extent map → decided `FMT_BLOCK` → read block 0 as XDB3 → XDD3 mismatch → dirty-trans cancel → shutdown. (`P56-FMT-BLOCK-RELOAD-PENDING ino=133 nextents=2` right before `xfs_dir3_block_verify` shutdown.)

**FIX (build `0273A7EB`, KEEP)** in `xfs/xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` fast-path dir-EX acquire (~L5429/L5511): also set `dir_ex_stale_refresh` when `MXFS_IF_DIR_RELOAD` is pending (bypassing the gen check and self_created gate), and clear/re-arm the flag around the reload — mirroring the consumer path.

**RESULT:** P56-BLKREAD 0×, P56-FMT-BLOCK-TORN 0×, **all dir3_block_verify/HOLE/FMT shutdowns eliminated.** The repro ran the full 300s (was round-1 shutdown); a clean instr=0 confirmation run had **zero shutdowns on all 16 nodes**.

**Residual blocker (next):** an intermittent **AGI unlinked-list** corruption — `xfs_iunlink+0x27c xfs_agi block 0x2` → trans_cancel via xfs_remove — a separate AG-metadata coherency root (cached AGI unlinked-bucket head goes stale under concurrent cross-node unlink). Existing handling at xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:11332 is the place to look next.

Current build on all 16 nodes: `A1F53770` (fix + P56 probes, gated behind `mxfs.dirwr`; remove before ship). The real `posix_semantics_multi16` criterion is **running now** (background task `bfj5bce86`) — its RESULT will be the first thing to check next session. Findings saved to memory `sess56-dir-format-coherency-fix-and-agi-residual`. **Criteria marker NOT written** — `posix_semantics_multi16` not yet confirmed PASS.

